cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PlanLab: a mechanism-switchable computational laboratory for planned-economy coordination"
abstract: >-
  A simulation core in which the coordination institution of an input-output economy
  is a replaceable module, used to compare material-balance planning, priority
  rationing, Lange-type price coordination, competitive markets and dual-track
  hybrids under controlled information delay and supply shocks.
message: "If you use this software or its scenario library, please cite the paper and the repository."
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
keywords:
  - input-output economics
  - material balance planning
  - shortage economy
  - computational experiment
  - delay differential equations
  - agent-based modelling
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: article
    title: "When an Economic Report Arrives Late: Feedback, production constraints and shortages in an input–output model"
    year: 2026
    notes: "Manuscript in preparation; see paper/main.pdf"
